notes.body:
@johnthacker

Thanks for the review!

I agree saving alongside the capture is problematic. I propose to move annotations into the user profile directory (e.g. \~/.config/wireshark/profiles/_\<profile\>_/annotations/) with a filename based on capture basename + a hash of the full path. To avoid popup warnings, I’ll store annotation edits in memory, mark the capture as having unsaved data, and only attempt to write when the user explicitly saves (or on close), similar to comments/time shifts. This should address temp files, read‑only paths, and shared captures while keeping a path toward pcapng integration later.

